      "The fare service gets route distance and time from the routing engine, applies the city rate card and the current surge multiplier for the pickup cell, and returns a quote with an ID and expiry so the shown price is honoured.",
      "Booking creates a trip in REQUESTED state using an idempotency key, so a double tap or retry never creates two trips; every state change is written with a version number.",
      "The matching engine pulls available drivers from the rider's H3 cell and surrounding rings, filters by vehicle type and status, ranks them by road ETA rather than straight-line distance, and may batch requests in short windows for better global assignment.",
      "The top driver gets a timed offer over a persistent socket with push fallback; acceptance is a conditional update (only if the trip is still unassigned and the driver is free), otherwise the next driver is offered.",
      "At pickup the rider tells the driver a short OTP; the trip moves to STARTED only if the OTP matches, which prevents wrong-rider and fake-start trips.",
      "During the trip the driver app streams GPS pings that update the geo index and feed the rider's live map, trip-sharing links and route-deviation checks.",
      "On drop the fare is computed from the quote rules plus allowed adjustments (route change, waiting, tolls), then collected by UPI, card, wallet or cash; cash trips post the platform commission to the driver's ledger.",
      "Both sides rate each other; cancellations after a grace window or driver arrival attract a fee per policy, and SOS alerts, emergency contacts and trip sharing are handled on a priority path."
