      "Students sign in with institute SSO and build a structured profile: academic records, backlogs, projects, skills and one or more resume versions generated from the profile fields.",
      "The placement cell verifies academic records with maker-checker approval, using university or DigiLocker-issued documents where available. Once verified, fields are locked, and any later edit reopens verification and is logged.",
      "Recruiters register a drive with role, CTC band, locations and eligibility criteria (branch, CGPA, backlogs, graduation year), and the placement cell approves it. The criteria are stored as a versioned rule set.",
      "When a drive is published, the eligibility engine evaluates verified data only and freezes a snapshot of the eligible list with the rule version. Notifications then go out through a queue, using DLT-registered SMS templates, email and in-app alerts.",
      "Eligible students opt in before the deadline and attach a resume version. Candidates take an online assessment through an integrated proctoring vendor, whose scores return by signed webhook.",
      "Shortlisted candidates are matched to panel slots using calendar APIs. The scheduler avoids clashes with the student's other drives and exams and records every reschedule with a reason.",
      "Each panelist submits rubric scores and a recommendation independently before seeing other panelists' scores. Submissions are locked, and any correction is appended as a new version.",
      "The offer service releases offers and records acceptance or decline. Acceptance runs a transactional one-offer check that updates the student's placement status and withdraws pending applications that the policy blocks.",
      "Placement statistics, such as placed versus eligible opted-in students and CTC distribution by branch, are computed from audit events. Each published number can be traced back to individual records."
