    "steps": [
      "The app sends the message over HTTPS; the edge layer terminates TLS, filters abuse and checks the session token, plan and account state before anything expensive runs.",
      "The chat service loads the conversation, custom instructions and any saved memory from the conversation store. OpenAI has publicly described running PostgreSQL with one primary and many read replicas on Azure for this kind of read-heavy load.",
      "Safety classifiers check the input (and later the output) against usage policies, the same family of checks OpenAI exposes as its Moderation API. Blocked or risky content gets a refusal or a safer completion path.",
      "The router picks a model. For GPT-5, OpenAI publicly described a real-time router that sends simple prompts to a fast model and hard ones to a reasoning model, depending on plan, load and explicit user choice.",
      "The inference fleet runs the model on GPU clusters, batching many users' requests together, and streams tokens back as server-sent events so the user sees text within seconds. The finished reply is written back to the conversation store.",
      "When the model emits a tool call, the tool runtime runs web search, a sandboxed code interpreter or file retrieval, then feeds the results back into the model's context before it continues streaming.",
      "API traffic enters through the developer platform: the gateway checks the API key, project and usage tier, and enforces requests-per-minute and tokens-per-minute limits. Token counts flow as usage events into billing and dashboards.",
      "On the operating side, research teams train and post-train new models and run capability and safety evals. Under the publicly described Preparedness Framework, frontier models are tested, including by external red teams, for risks such as bio, cyber and self-improvement before release, and the results go into a published system card.",
      "Launches are staged: features and models are turned on by flag, often for paid tiers or a share of users first, then widened while metrics are watched. OpenAI's publicly described 'iterative deployment' approach means rolling back when needed, as with the April 2025 GPT-4o sycophancy update."
    ]
