      "Build and sign: the developer builds in Xcode (locally or with Xcode Cloud) against the current SDK; the binary is signed with an Apple-issued certificate and provisioning profile, so the device can verify who made it and that it was not altered.",
      "Upload: the signed archive goes to App Store Connect with metadata, screenshots, age rating, privacy nutrition labels and the required privacy manifest; automated checks flag missing entitlements or disallowed API usage.",
      "Beta: TestFlight distributes the build to internal testers immediately and to external testers after a beta review, returning crash logs and feedback to the developer.",
      "App Review: the release candidate is checked against the publicly published App Review Guidelines for safety, performance, business rules, design and legal or privacy issues; rejections come back with guideline references and can be appealed.",
      "Publish: an approved version is released manually, automatically or on a date, and the App Store catalog updates the listing, search index and regional availability.",
      "Download: the user taps Get, the App Store app authenticates the Apple Account, and the CDN serves a device-specific thinned build; iOS verifies the signature before install.",
      "Purchase: in-app purchases and subscriptions go through StoreKit, which returns cryptographically signed transactions; the app's server should verify them and listen to App Store Server Notifications for renewals and refunds.",
      "Update and sync: new versions reach devices through automatic updates, optionally as a phased release that can be paused; app data syncs across the user's devices through iCloud and CloudKit, with end-to-end encryption for more categories when Advanced Data Protection is on.",
      "How Apple ships: Apple publicly announces each year's OS at WWDC in June, ships developer betas and a public beta over the summer, and releases in the autumn alongside new iPhones; its publicly described functional organisation and privacy-by-design reviews shape features before they reach this pipeline."
