      "Months before the sale, teams forecast demand, plan capacity, and run repeated production-like load tests and failure drills; a feature freeze is publicly described as locking down changes in the run-up so the sale runs on tested code.",
      "At sale start, the CDN serves static assets and cached pages while edge rules rate-limit, filter bots and shed excess load before it reaches origin services.",
      "A virtual queue (waiting room) admits shoppers to hot deals at the rate the backend was tested for, giving fair ordering and a clear wait message instead of errors.",
      "Catalogue, deal and price data are pre-warmed into in-memory caches so browsing barely touches primary databases; price is re-verified at checkout so a stale cache never sets the charge.",
      "The inventory service reserves a unit with an atomic conditional decrement (only if stock is greater than zero) and attaches a time-limited hold, so stock can never go negative.",
      "Checkout uses an idempotency key per order and hands off to payment for UPI, cards or EMI; failed or abandoned payments release the hold, and COD orders skip online payment after eligibility checks.",
