      "The desktop agent watches the file system, splits a changed file into fixed-size chunks (for example 4 MB), hashes each chunk with SHA-256, and sends the ordered hash list plus the base revision it edited from.",
      "The upload service opens a resumable session keyed by an upload ID; each chunk upload is idempotent, so after a network drop the client asks which chunks were received and resumes from there.",
      "For each hash the service checks the chunk index; only chunks not already stored are uploaded to object storage, which gives cross-version and (if allowed) cross-user deduplication.",
      "Before any write or read, the ACL service resolves the user's effective permission on the file, including permissions inherited from shared parent folders.",
      "Once all chunks are durable, the metadata service commits a new file version (chunk list, size, hash, author, timestamp) in a single transaction, but only if the client's base revision is still the latest; otherwise it saves the upload as a conflicted copy.",
      "The same transaction appends an entry with a monotonically increasing sequence number to the namespace's change journal, so every change is ordered and replayable.",
      "The notification service tells online devices subscribed to that namespace that something changed; the notification carries no file data, only a hint to sync.",
      "Each device calls list-changes with its last cursor, applies the returned entries in order, and downloads only chunks it does not already have locally via short-lived signed URLs.",
      "Deletes move files to trash with a retention window; background jobs purge expired trash and old versions, decrement chunk reference counts, and delete chunks from object storage only when no version references them."
