    "steps": [
      "The customer's message reaches the chat API, which redacts phone numbers, emails and account IDs and classifies intent. Account-specific questions (my bill, my balance) are marked to bypass the cache because their answers are personal.",
      "For FAQ intents, the redacted query is embedded and searched in the cache index, filtered by language and customer segment (for example prepaid vs postpaid). A hit above the tuned similarity threshold, whose linked article versions are still current, is returned immediately.",
      "On a miss, a LangChain agent built with create_agent and init_chat_model calls a retriever tool over the KB vector store. response_format forces a structured result: answer, cited article IDs, confidence and a needs_human flag; PIIMiddleware and model fallback middleware wrap the model calls.",
      "The confidence gate sends a grounded, cited answer to the customer. If the intent is generic and confidence is high, it writes the query vector, answer, segment and cited article IDs with versions into the cache, with a TTL as a backstop.",
      "If confidence is low, no article supports the answer, the customer asks for a person, or the question needs account access, the chat is handed to a human agent. The agent sees the thread history saved by the checkpointer so the customer does not repeat themselves.",
      "When an editor publishes, edits or retires an article in the CMS, a webhook emits a change event with the article ID and new version onto a queue.",
      "The reindex worker re-chunks and re-embeds the changed article in the KB vector store, then deletes every cache entry tagged with that article ID. Purging is done before or together with the reindex so no stale answer survives the change.",
      "Tracing records cache hit/miss, similarity scores, handoffs and customer feedback. Sampled cache hits and human resolution labels are reviewed to tune the threshold and catch false hits."
    ]
