      "The traveller's request reaches the graph on LangSmith Agent Server under a thread_id per trip. The StateGraph has a typed state with messages, trip constraints, flight_hold, hotel_hold, quote and approval keys; messages uses a list reducer so agents append rather than overwrite.",
      "The flight agent reads stored preferences from PostgresStore under a namespace such as (\"travellers\", user_id). It searches and holds a fare through tools, then returns Command(goto=\"hotel_agent\", update={\"flight_hold\": ...}) to hand off with the hold recorded in shared state.",
      "The hotel agent uses the flight arrival and departure times from state to search and hold a room. If the dates cannot work, it hands back to the flight agent with a Command(goto=\"flight_agent\") and a reason. Otherwise it hands off to payments.",
      "The payments agent re-checks both holds, builds a single quote with a version number, the total and the currency, and writes it to state. No charge happens in this node.",
      "A dedicated approval node calls interrupt() with the exact itinerary and quote. The checkpointer persists the paused run. The traveller later answers through Command(resume={\"approved\": true, \"quote_version\": n}), and the node routes on that answer.",
