      "The Agent Server receives the application and starts a run on a thread whose thread_id is the application ID; the graph is compiled with a Postgres checkpointer so every super-step is saved.",
      "The document intake node uses an LLM to extract fields (identity, employer, declared income) from uploaded documents into the typed state, and validates them against a schema before moving on.",
      "Bureau check and income verification run as parallel branches in the same super-step, each writing to its own state key; both external calls carry an idempotency key derived from the application ID so a retry never triggers a second inquiry.",
      "The risk scoring node combines bureau data, verified income and policy rules into a score with reason codes; hard policy stops are deterministic rules, not model output.",
      "A conditional edge routes clear approvals and clear declines straight to finalize, and sends edge cases (borderline score, mismatched income, thin file) to the underwriter review node.",
      "The review node calls interrupt() with a case summary; the run pauses and its state is checkpointed. The underwriter decides in the credit UI, which resumes the same thread_id with Command(resume={decision, reason, reviewer_id}).",
      "The finalize node records the decision, reason codes and reviewer, then books the loan or sends the decline notice through the loan system using an idempotent request keyed by application ID.",
