    "steps": [
      "The analyst, or an API client on Agent Server, starts a run with a list of document IDs and a thread_id. The checkpointer keys all state for this run to that thread_id.",
      "The load_docs node fetches each report from storage, extracts the text, and writes a list of {doc_id, title, text} items to state. Very large reports are split into sections, and each section is treated as its own item.",
      "A conditional edge function returns [Send(\"summarise_doc\", {\"doc\": d}) for d in state[\"docs\"]]. This creates one task per document, and each task gets only its own per-item input rather than the full graph state.",
      "The summarise_doc tasks run in parallel in the same super-step, capped by max_concurrency in the run config. Each task calls the model with structured output and returns {\"summaries\": [{doc_id, key_points, figures}]}, and a RetryPolicy on the node handles transient model errors.",
      "The summaries key is declared as Annotated[list, operator.add], so the parallel writes are concatenated instead of conflicting. The Postgres checkpointer saves state after the super-step. If one branch fails, the writes from branches that finished are kept as pending writes, so a resume only re-runs the failed branch.",
      "A budget check compares the total token size of the summaries with the reduce model's context budget. If they do not fit, it groups the summaries and sends the groups back through summarisation as a collapse pass. Otherwise it routes to write_brief.",
      "The write_brief reduce node turns all summaries into one brief and tags every claim and figure with its doc_id. It also verifies that every input doc_id appears in the summaries, so a missing document is reported instead of silently dropped.",
      "A review node calls interrupt() with the draft, and the analyst approves or edits it through Command(resume=...). The approved brief is returned, and progress is streamed to the UI with the updates stream mode."
    ]
