      "The student sends a message from the web UI with the session's thread_id, which is one thread per tutoring session. The client opens a run stream with stream_mode set to messages, updates and custom.",
      "The Agent Server loads the latest checkpoint for that thread_id from the Postgres checkpointer. The new message is appended to state through the add_messages reducer, so earlier turns are preserved.",
      "The diagnose node reads the student's profile from PostgresStore under the namespace (\"students\", student_id). It classifies intent and level, and the resulting state delta arrives in updates mode for the UI to render as a progress step.",
      "A conditional edge reads the intent from state and routes to the tutor node (explain), the hint node (stuck) or the answer checker (answer submitted).",
      "The tutor node calls a streaming chat model. Messages mode emits (token chunk, metadata) pairs, and the UI appends only chunks whose langgraph_node metadata is the tutor node.",
      "The hint node calls get_stream_writer() and writes a structured payload such as a hint type and hint level. The payload arrives in custom mode, and the UI shows it as a separate hint card instead of chat text.",
      "The answer checker grades the submission. If it needs a follow-up, the ask node calls interrupt() with a question, the run pauses with its state checkpointed, and the student's reply resumes it through Command(resume=...).",
      "The progress writer updates mastery in the store so that later sessions on new threads can use it. Because every super-step is checkpointed, a refresh or reconnect resumes from the thread's latest state.",
      "For review, teachers or developers use get_state_history on the thread to replay a session. They can also fork from an earlier checkpoint with update_state to test a different tutoring path."
