    "steps": [
      "The user signs in to the web app and uploads a PDF or asks a question; the backend resolves the tenant and holds the Langflow API key server-side, never in the browser.",
      "On upload, the backend stores the PDF in object storage and calls POST /api/v1/run/<ingest-flow-id>, using tweaks to set the file input component's path and the document's tenant and document ids as metadata.",
      "The ingest flow loads the PDF, splits it into overlapping chunks, embeds each chunk with the embedding model component, and upserts vectors into the vector store under the tenant's collection or namespace, set via tweak.",
      "For a question, the backend calls POST /api/v1/run/<chat-flow-id> with input_value, input_type and output_type set to chat, a session_id per conversation, and tweaks that pin the vector store component to that tenant's scope.",
      "The vector store component in the chat flow runs a similarity search with the question and returns the top-k chunks with their metadata (document, page).",
      "A small custom component checks retrieval scores and chunk count; if nothing relevant is found, the flow returns a fixed 'not found in your documents' message instead of calling the model.",
      "The prompt component combines the system instructions, retrieved chunks with source labels, and recent turns from message history for the same session_id.",
      "The chat model component generates an answer restricted to the context and cites sources; the chat output returns it, and the backend parses the run response and renders the answer with page references.",
      "Tracing to Langfuse or LangSmith records each run's retrieved chunks, prompt, latency and token use so the team can debug bad answers and compare flow versions."
    ]
