    "title": "Agent component with tools",
    "summary": "A Langflow Agent answers operations questions by choosing among a calculator, URL fetch, API Request and a runbook flow used as a tool, and it is tested in the Playground before being called over the API. It must never invent numbers or system status that did not come from a tool call, and it must never take a write action against production systems.",
    "industry": "IT operations",
    "problem": "On-call engineers lose time jumping between status pages, internal APIs, runbooks and spreadsheets to answer routine questions such as error-budget math or the current health of a service. A plain chatbot cannot reach those sources and tends to guess.",
