    "steps": [
      "An external scheduler (cron, a CI job or a workflow orchestrator) fires on a fixed interval, because the refresh is driven from outside the flow rather than by a chat message.",
      "The scheduler calls POST /api/v1/run/<flow-id> with an API key and tweaks that override component settings for this run, such as the source path, target collection name or a full-reindex flag.",
      "A custom change-detector component lists source files, computes a content hash per file and compares it with the ingest manifest. It passes only new or changed files forward and emits delete instructions for files that no longer exist.",
      "File loader components read each selected file and return text plus basic source details. Unsupported or empty files are recorded as skipped instead of failing the whole run.",
      "A custom metadata component, a Python class with inputs and outputs, attaches doc_id, source path, title, document type, version or modified time, content hash, embedding model name and access or tenant tags to every document.",
      "The text splitter component breaks documents into chunks with a chosen size and overlap. Each chunk inherits the document metadata and gets a deterministic chunk id built from doc_id and chunk index.",
      "The embeddings model component embeds chunks in batches. Batches that fail after retries are written to a failed-docs list so the next run can pick them up.",
      "The vector store component deletes old chunks for each changed doc_id and upserts the new chunks by id, with metadata stored alongside each vector so retrieval flows can filter on it.",
      "The manifest is updated with the new hash and status per document. A run report with added, updated, deleted, skipped and failed counts is sent to the team, and traces are available in LangSmith or Langfuse."
    ]
